model {
  extend basalt.toolsGateway {
    metadata {
      constraint "The tools service serves the pool app's source for its own origin, the one its own pool calls use, derived from the stage. Whatever host the bundle was built for, the served deployment file and font links name that origin, so the pool provider declares this stack's host and an installed pool's token reaches no other stack. The served version stays the bundle's own hash: the host the bundle was built for serves it byte for byte and rolls nothing out, and pools a stack installed earlier from a bundle built for another host keep their source until the bundle next changes. A local e2e host keeps its own local origin, an already-local recipe peer and its own version. A seed without exactly one pool origin declaration fails as retryable storage unavailability with a logged reason."
    }
  }
}
